# GH issue #156: this directory must exist on the host (and therefore in
# the ./eval:/app/eval:ro read-only bind mount - see docker-compose.yaml)
# BEFORE the container starts. `adk eval` writes its own local run-history
# bookkeeping here at runtime; docker-compose.yaml mounts a writable named
# volume (adk_eval_history) at this exact path so that write succeeds
# despite the parent mount being read-only - but Docker can only attach
# that volume mount onto an EXISTING directory node inside a read-only
# mount, not create one (attempting to led to "read-only file system"
# trying to mkdir the mountpoint itself). This placeholder is what makes
# the directory exist in the first place; its actual contents are never
# read (the named volume's contents are what the container sees, not this
# repo checkout's).
